Z||000000||johnt671||02-22-2001||03:23 PM||||2 problems: 84 fiero se 2m4 4 cyl w/air: first is slow starting.  cranks until oil pressure lite goes out then starts.  book said the relay is bad and the computer starts the fuel pump when thr o p lite goes out.  i replaced the relay and checked the fuse, and both failed to correct problem. belive the relay is one of four on the drivers side of the engine compartment.  2nd is the cooling fan.  works when air is on but not when the air is off.  have replaced the fan switch w/ a used one and can't find the relay.  fuse is good<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GT||02-22-2001||07:27 PM||||I have a 87GT and the fan relay I believe is on the passenger side up in the front compartment.  Its hiding under there somewhere.  I dont know if it is the same on the 84s.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-22-2001||08:50 PM||||If the fan works at all the realy is good. Unless you have the 2 speed fan... then you have 2 relays and 2 coolant switches. theres an article in my cave about the fans in the engine area. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||02-22-2001||10:14 PM||||The fan will come on anytime the AC is on and the vehicle's speed is below 35 mph.  If your  fan switch is still stock, it wont come on normally until the coolant is 235 degrees (ouch).  Not a good design, but Rodney Dickman has a new 205 on/ 195 degree off rad. fan switch that will work in your car.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||02-23-2001||07:17 PM||||thanks for your help.  i may try the lower temp switch.  thought i saw a 160 degree switch and thermostat on rodney dickman's site and may try that.  also goying in theorgre" cave to see what's in there. thanks again||||reg||10
